course: dictionary
lesson: 2860
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary can give more than one meaning for a word. Dolphin has two numbered meanings: a clever sea mammal with a curved fin, or a kind that lives in rivers.
explain: Context decides which meaning fits. «Dolphins find things by echolocation» is about the sea mammal, so you can tell which meaning the writer means. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Context clues can also explain a phrase. In «a bottlenose dolphin», the word bottlenose names a kind of dolphin, and «a pod of dolphins» tells you that a pod is a group.
fact: A dolphin is a mammal, not a fish: it breathes air through a blowhole.
fact: Dolphins find food by echolocation: they send out fast clicks and listen to the echoes.
fact: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, invented as a calf.»
fact: «Dolphins sleep with half of their brain at a time, switching sides, so they can keep coming up to breathe.»
fact: A group of dolphins is called a pod.
exercise: A dolphin breathes through its blowhole. What does a dolphin breathe? | Sand | Water | Mud | *Air
exercise: «Dolphins find things by echolocation.» What do dolphins listen for? | Songs from fish | *Echoes from clicks they send out | Whistles from other boats | Waves on the shore
exercise: Lisa reads «a pod of dolphins». What does pod mean? | A type of boat | A hidden cave | A single fin | *A group
test: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, invented as a calf.» What is a calf here? | A small boat | *A baby dolphin | A rock in the sea | A fish's fin
test: Is a dolphin a fish or a mammal? Use the clue that it breathes air through a blowhole. | Fish | Insect | *Mammal | Reptile
exam: Why do dolphins sleep with half of their brain at a time? | So they can grow a longer snout | *So they can keep coming up to breathe | So they can hide from sharks | So they can catch fish faster
